    "chunk_size_bytes": 1527,
    "chunk_text": "One important area we are focusing on is corruption. Corruption is not simply about a person taking public money, but it also affects the entire development process, increases cost, weakens institutions, damages public confidence and makes honest businesses less willing to compete and invest. Therefore, our objective must be broader than investigating individual incidents; we must create institutions where transparency, accountability and integrity become normal features in public administration. For example, yesterday, we witnessed a very unusual situation. A news was reported earlier, weeks back, relating to a matter connected with money laundering and a number of arrests were made yesterday with regard to that. So, these are part and parcel of the reforms we are making at the moment. We are highly committed to establish a transparent and a corruption-free business environment. That is the direction President Anura Kumara Dissanayake and this Government are moving towards.\n\nInvestigations into the Easter Sunday attacks also remain an important national responsibility. The victim families are still waiting for answers. Therefore, the Government has a duty to ensure that every credible lead is followed, every evidence is examined into and no political considerations stand between the victims and the truth. We should neither predetermine conclusions nor allow serious unanswered questions to disappear with time. Accountability must come through credible investigation and proper administration of justice."
