    "chunk_size_bytes": 1921,
    "chunk_text": "(a) what steps the Government is taking to address the concerns of the Sri Lankan Tamil refugees in India who wish to return to Sri Lanka, particularly regarding security clearance, housing, access to land and property, employment, reparations and rebuilding their lives, especially in light of the arrest in May, 2025 of a 75-year-old Sri Lankan Tamil refugee upon his return through Palaly Airport after living in India for several decades;\n\nHon. Speaker, I saw that recently the Government has taken a new decision in this regard. So, I would like the Hon. Minister to tell us what it is.\n\n(c) what steps must a refugee take before returning to Sri Lanka, including with regard to the requirements for verification of nationality, travel documents and security clearance;\n\n(d) how many Sri Lankan refugees have returned from India to Sri Lanka in each year from 2009 to date, separately identifying those who returned with UNHCR assistance and those who returned independently;\n\n(e) what the security clearance process under the new procedure is, including -\n\n(i) which institution or institutions conduct the clearance;\n\n(ii) what criteria are applied and what information or documents are required;\n\n(iii) the maximum time frame within which the assessment must be completed;\n\n(iv) what happens if security clearance is refused;\n\n247 248\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n(v) whether reasons must be provided for an adverse decision and whether the person has a right to seek a review or appeal; and\n\n(vi) what safeguards exist against arbitrary or indefinite security screening;\n\n(f) what assistance will be provided to returning refugees regarding land, housing, property, reparations, employment and livelihoods; and\n\n(g) whether the Government will establish a One-Stop Return and Reintegration Unit in the North and the East to resolve these matters through a single mechanism, and if not, why?"
