    "chunk_text": "\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0db8\u0dda \u0d9a\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Minister, the Hon. Speaker is saying that your answer in response to my question should be quick.\n\n397 398\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 1\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf \u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2 \u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8 \u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf ]\n\n2026 \u0dad\u0daf\u0d9c \u0dca\u0dae\u0dd4 20\n\n\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca\u0da7 \u0da2\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Okay, I will be quick.\n\nSir, it is not that I did not answer Question No. 1, but I answered it. The data was from 2021 to 2025.\n\nYour second Supplementary Question was about the net foreign contribution. In the past also, we had been dealing with such a situation. Now, we are focusing more on the net value addition. Specially, when it comes to garment and other industries, of course, the value addition is relatively low. We are moving onto other areas as well. - [Interruption.] Yes, that is it. The net foreign contribution comes in investments, earnings et cetera. So, it varies; it is not limited to one area. So, we focus on diversity of these investments, maybe, in earnings or investments.\n\nThen, with regard to the labour force, we are moving ahead with the promotion of the traditional labour force, while increasing their competency to match the global demand. Those people are not leaving the country, but we are placing our labour in strategically important places. So, as a result, our foreign remittances will also go up.\n\nSir, during the last seven-month period, more than US Dollars 5 billion had been remitted to Sri Lanka. It is more likely that the same pattern would continue. So, by the year end, we could easily hit that target of US Dollars 9 billion as well. Therefore, we will pay attention to our labour force."
