f\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0b95\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0baf\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bb5 \u0b8e\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b95\u0ba4\u0baf\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd;\n\n\u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b87\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0b95\u0baa\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b85\u0bb1\u0bbf\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bbe?\n\n(\u0b86) \u0b87\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb1\u0bb2\u0bcd, \u0b8f\u0ba9\u0bcd? asked the Minister of Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Co-operative Development:\n\n(a) Will he inform this House the - (i) number of Co-operative Rural Banks currently operating in Sri Lanka; (ii) names of those banks; (iii) number of Rural Banks among them which have collapsed during the period from the year 2000 to date; (iv) names of the said banks; (v) number of depositors who have been affected by that situation; (vi) reliefs granted to the said depositors by the Department of Co-operative Development; and (vii) measures that will be taken to conduct formal investigations into the financial frauds of those banks and to enforce the law against the persons responsible for them?\n\n(b) If not, why?"
