    "chunk_size_bytes": 1367,
    "chunk_text": "Transfer of Fishery Harbour \u2022 Cabinet Decision No.16/2061/725/009-I dated 26.10.2016 approved the transfer of Lots 01 and 04 of the Oluvil Fishery Harbour to the Ministry of Fisheries. \u2022 An MoU between SLPA and the Ministry of Fisheries was signed on 09.05.2022 to formalize the transfer. \u2022 The facilities were intended to be operated as a fishery harbour.\n\nCalling for EoI/RFP for the long-term lease of lands and buildings belonging to Sri Lanka Ports Authority at Oluvil for port-related industries/ business ventures\n\n7. Yes. According to the information provided by the Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management Department, revetments comprising armour boulders have been constructed along approximately 16.5 kilometres of the coastline to mitigate coastal erosion occurring in the vicinity of Oluvil Port. Furthermore, the Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management Department has informed that an annual allocation of\n\n819 820\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0d9c\u0dda \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n\u0db1\u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db1\u0d9c\u0dca\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\n\napproximately Rs. 57 million will be provided for the implementation of coastal protection and maintenance measures to address the erosion issues associated with Oluvil Port."
