    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "84bc5d5b3370562c9150e8b6d5d18ab0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2213,
    "chunk_text": "Then, Sri Lanka ranks 20th globally for cyberspace-related threats. There are 9.1 million distinct cyber threats detected in a single year. Sir, children's sexual abuse material availability rate is 27.8 per 10,000 people, which is a very dangerous phenomena. There is a lot of data on these issues.\n\nAlso, today, various forms of activities are going on, on the Internet. Drugs are obtained through the Internet and people commit suicide because of the addiction to Internet. Earlier, children used to go out and play - we used to go out and play - but, today, the phone has become the child\u2019s best friend. Psychologists have said that phone addiction is a problem because, then, you do not need people, you do not socialize and thereby, you become a loner and suffer from mental issues.\n\nTherefore, I respectfully beg this House - I spoke to the Minister also - that we should collectively and expeditiously bring in a Bill to address this issue.\n\n931 932\n\n\u0db1\u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db1\u0d9c\u0dca\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\n\n\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, your time is up.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dc6\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db8\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dad\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0b95\u0baa\u0bb8\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bc1\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe) (The Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, PC) Please give me half a minute more, Sir.\n\nWith this Bill getting delayed, each day a child would get abused, a child\u2019s photographs would be put on social media and a child would meet somebody through social media and be subjected to various forms of sexual harassment. Therefore, compared to any other Bill, this Bill would be more important, if we are to protect our children in the future. The world has changed; today, technology dictates everything. Therefore, I humbly beg this House, through this Adjournment Motion, that we all should collectively and expeditiously bring in a Bill in this regard, whereby there would be restrictions imposed on the use of Internet by children.\n\nThank you."
  },
