    "chunk_text": "This cooperation may include the exchange of knowledge, information, good practices, technical materials and expertise, capacity development and training programmes, exchange of government officials and experts, study tours, organization of joint workshops and seminars, and consultations between relevant officials and subject experts. Furthermore, feasibility studies, e-readiness assessments, institutional cooperation, public-private sector linkages,\n\n(iv) Progress made to date in implementing the said Agreement under the following programmes, discussions are underway to initiate some more tasks.\n\n1. The India-Sri Lanka NASSCOM Programme\n\nThe India-Sri Lanka NASSCOM - NaSCoM - DISHA Mentorship Programme is a digital-economy cooperation initiative under which India\u2019s National Association of Software and Service Companies - NASSCOM - has extended its flagship Tech SME Mentorship Programme \u201cDISHA\u201d to Sri Lankan technology Small and Medium Enterprises - SMEs - for the first time outside India. Launched in July, 2026 in Colombo by the High Commission of India in collaboration with SLASSCOM and local stakeholders, the programme provides structured, high-impact mentorship to 48 selected Sri Lankan tech SMEs, with guidance from NASSCOM experts and Indian industry leaders on strategy, growth planning, organizational development and market access, thereby strengthening the capacity and global competitiveness of Sri Lanka\u2019s ICT/BPM sector and deepening India-Sri Lanka cooperation in the digital economy.\n\n2. \"GatiShakti\" Programme"
