    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, I saw the update where the Minister had said that over 250 parcels of land belonged to the military have been released, but we have not seen that happen on the ground. I know, there are a couple of lands that have been released in Batticaloa, one land in Ampara and a road has also been opened up in Vasavilan. But, in Palaly, people are protesting for the tenth consecutive week and in Myliddy and Keppapilavu in\n\n(f) What commitment has the Government communicated internationally regarding an immediate moratorium on the PTA, the release of political prisoners and its repeal?\n\nThe High Commissioner's statement, Sir, very explicitly states that the proposed draft law is far worse than the existing PTA. I do not know why the Government media channels and the Government Representatives who welcome and try to claim mileage out of it are not saying that. The High Commissioner has explicitly said that the Protection of the State from Terrorism Act, the PSTA, or whatever your draft law is, is far worse than the existing PTA.\n\n(g) What position and timetable has the Government communicated to the UN regarding the Provincial Councils Elections, the promised new Constitution and meaningful devolution?\n\nFor the guarantee of non-recurrence of the issues faced, Sir, there needs to be a political solution, where political power is shared. We see no progress on that. I am a Member of the Parliamentary Select Committee appointed to go into the electoral system for Provincial Council Elections to be held, and it is a time-wasting exercise. We have very clearly said that the Government's intention is to delay elections using the Select Committee. Meaningful devolution could, obviously, happen, if there is a new Constitution and that is when we can talk about it, which is highly unlikely."
