    "chunk_size_bytes": 1871,
    "chunk_text": "(iii) In June 2025, the Joint Technical Teams - JTTs - of India and Sri Lanka convened in India to discuss on the technical parameters of the proposed grid interconnection. Most of the base technical parameters were widely discussed and agreed at the meeting.\n\n(v) This will improve the grid stability and reliability through an additional international electricity connection and it integrates Sri Lanka into the regional electricity market, creating possibilities for wider cross-border electricity trading.\n\n(vi) (i) High Capital Expenditure: As per the\n\nestimates, the cost for the project is approximately US Dollars 1.24 billion, presenting a substantial financing challenge.\n\n(ii) Unresolved Commercial Frameworks:\n\nThe definitive financial, commercial and power purchase arrangements between the two nations remain to be finalized.\n\n(iii) Domestic Transmission Infrastructure\n\nUpgrades: Integrating the connection requires major grid reinforcement within Sri Lanka, specifically a 220/400 kV HVDC converter station at Mannar and high-voltage transmission links connecting to the National Grid.\n\n(iv) Submarine Cable Technical Complexities: Laying the subsea cable across the Palk Strait introduces significant deep-water marine engineering and technical complexities.\n\n(v) Socio-Cultural and Religious Sensitivities: The proposed cable route traverses the geographically and historically sensitive Madurai-to-Mannar corridor, which holds profound cultural and religious significance.\n\n(vi) Environmental and System Integration\n\nAssessments: Comprehensive impact studies are required to address the marine environmental considerations of the submarine route, alongside detailed technical assessments of the two distinct national electricity grids.\n\n(b) Not applicable.\n\n1149 1150\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf] ]\n\n\u0dc3\u0dd0.\u0dba\u0dd4."
