    "chunk_size_bytes": 1929,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 (\u0dc0\u0dc0\u0daf\u0dba) \u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0db4\u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dc4\u0dc3 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf) (\u0bc7\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb5\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbe\u0bbe\u0bcd) \u0bbe\u0bbf\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bbf - \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Dr.) Rizvie Salih - Deputy Speaker and Chair of Committees) Hon. Speaker, I wish to speak on the Determination under the Women Empowerment Act, No. 37 of 2024. - [Interruption.]\n\nThe Women Empowerment Act takes our approach beyond the traditional concept of protecting women. It speaks of empowerment, and empowerment means much more than protection; it means that a woman should have the opportunity to learn, work, earn, participate, make decisions, seek justice and determine the course of her own life. - [Interruption.]\n\nSir, the Act establishes an important institutional framework. It provides for the National Commission on Women, the formulation and implementation of a National Policy on the advancement and empowerment of women, mechanisms for the protection of women\u2019s rights and an Ombudsperson for Women\u2019s Rights.\n\nThe Commission has substantial responsibilities including receiving and investigating complaints concerning violation of women\u2019s rights, conducting inquiries, making recommendations for law reform, assessing the impact of legislation and policies and\n\n1219 1220\n\n\u0db4\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dda\u0db8\u0dca\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\n\npromoting awareness of women\u2019s rights. Will this institution deliver what the women of Sri Lanka want? This is the real test before us. Sir, this is a very important topic before us. It concerns more than 50 per cent of the population of this nation and the rights that they are entitled to and the benefits they could reap because it is their right once again."
  },
