    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "3279a235e6f33375ba81e289ca974128",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1231,
    "chunk_text": "promoting awareness of women\u2019s rights. Will this institution deliver what the women of Sri Lanka want? This is the real test before us. Sir, this is a very important topic before us. It concerns more than 50 per cent of the population of this nation and the rights that they are entitled to and the benefits they could reap because it is their right once again.\n\nHon. Speaker and Hon. Members of the House, there is the woman living in Colombo and the woman living in a remote village. They are not a homogenous group. Among them, there is the plantation worker, the factory worker, the professional, the entrepreneur, the woman working abroad to sustain her family, the single mother, the elderly woman and the woman living with a disability. And, there are women who, because of poverty, social circumstance and other vulnerabilities, may not even know where to turn to when their rights are violated. If this legislation is to achieve its full purpose, the benefits must reach each one of them. We must be unequivocal in this matter.\n\nWe must also know that harassment of women is not a minor inconvenience, and discrimination is not something that a woman should be told just to tolerate, as they have been told through ages."
  },
