    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24342_english_2026-09-10.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-10-2026-09-10-0093",
    "chunk_index": 93,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "9c37d8edca9ac3f77261978822b0639c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1979,
    "chunk_text": "The Act also recognizes particular needs of women with disabilities. We must, therefore, ensure that women's empowerment is not only reflected in our economic policies and employment policies, but also in our financial inclusion programmes and in national development strategies that we may formulate.\n\nSir, this is an important administrative provision that has been provided for in the Act. At the same time, we must ensure that the remuneration provided is adequate to attract persons with necessary competence, experience and integrity, while being administered with transparency and proper accountability.\n\nThe National Commission on Women is not able to function alone and isolated. The Ministry responsible for women and child affairs, the Police, the Judiciary, the Attorney-General\u2019s Department, legal aid services, provincial and local authorities, educational institutions, the civil society and community organizations, all have important roles to play. I would add one more institution of paramount importance and that is the family because laws can punish and institutions can protect, but lasting social change requires a change in attitudes, which begin from our very homes. We must create workplaces where harassment is unacceptable, schools where girls are encouraged to lead and communities where a woman seeking help is supported rather than stigmatized.\n\nSir, this Act was passed in 2024. We must, now, ensure that the machinery created by this Act becomes fully functional, visible and accessible. The National Commission on Women must become an institution that women know about. Sir, let us build a Sri Lanka where a woman\u2019s opportunity is not determined by her gender, where her safety is not dependent upon her social status, where her economic future is not limited by outdated expectations, where her voice is not diminished because she is a woman and where leadership is determined by her ability, integrity, commitment and service to the people."
  },
