    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "50d5e5aa0f7518070fbbfb91c0cc2345",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1190,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Presiding Member, today, we are discussing the Determination under the Women Empowerment Act, which relates to the National Commission on Women. I congratulate the Hon. Minister of Women and Child Affairs for presenting this Determination relating to the National Commission on Women. I was told that women in Sri Lanka had been struggling for nearly 30 years to get this Commission operationalized.\n\nThe Government must ensure that the National Budget is gender-responsive. It will also try to change the discriminatory social attitudes. The Government cannot achieve gender equality through laws alone; it must be done through schools, the media, religious and community leaders, workplaces, political parties and public institutions. The Government must change the attitude of looking upon women as inferior and attitudes which restrict their participation in social activities. It will protect the vulnerable and disadvantaged women and address issues of women who face multiple disadvantages, women-headed households, women with disabilities, older women, poor rural women, plantation sector women, woman migrant workers and women affected by disasters, conflict and displacement."
  },
