    "chunk_size_bytes": 2102,
    "chunk_text": "2021 10,000,000.00 1,759,664.00 8,240,336.00\n\n2022 1,500,000.00 697,407.95 802,592.05\n\n2023 3,000,000.00 2,939,423.40 60,576.60\n\n2024 10,000,000.00 4,896,114.38 5,103,885.62\n\n2025 25,000,000.00 8,847,828.93 16,152,171.07\n\n(vii) The TMK computer software was developed with the objective of identifying medical lineages and establishing an information database containing comprehensive data on medical practitioners. Of the information relating to approximately 6,000 medical practitioners received at the provincial level, the details of nearly 2,000 practitioners have been entered into the TMK computer software to date. It is planned to analyse the data based on the information entered into the system in order to accurately identify the respective medical lineages. Furthermore, in order to preserve medical books, equipment and other relevant materials of medical value possessed by traditional indigenous medical practitioners,\n\n\u2022 Audio-visual programmes documenting the medical treatments provided by traditional medical practitioners belonging to the verified traditional medical lineages have been produced and preserved.\n\n\u2022 A museum has been established on the premises of the Bandaranaike Memorial Ayurveda Research Institute.\n\n1337 1338\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc3(\u0dc0\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0dba)\u0dc3 \u0dd2\u0dca\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0da2\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dae\u0dca\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n2026 \u0dca\u0dd0\u0dda\u0dad\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0d9a\u0dc3\u0dc310\u0dc3\n\n\u2022 Rare palm-leaf manuscripts of significant medical value that were in a state of deterioration have been physically restored, re-bound using cords and threads, classified, entered into a database and documented.\n\n\u2022 Eight hundred and sixteen palm-leaf manuscripts so preserved have been scanned and preserved using digital technology.\n\n\u2022 Of the rare palm-leaf manuscripts that had undergone treatment with natural colouring materials and physical restoration, 10 manuscripts were selected and transcribed and 100 copies of each manuscript were printed and distributed among Central Government hospitals and provincial Ayurveda libraries.\n\nTMK Project\n\n(viii) The financial progress is set out in (vii) above."
