    "chunk_text": "(iii) \u0b87\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b95\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b8e\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0ba3\u0baf\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc8\u0baf\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b85\u0b95\u0bc7\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b9f\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbe\u0b95 \u0b87\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0b95\u0bb0 \u0b8e\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4 \u0ba4\u0bc0\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bc7\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b8e\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc8.\n\n(\u0b87) \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bc7\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0ba4\u0bc1.\n\n(a) (i) Yes.\n\n(ii) 1. The Ministry of Energy to represent the\n\nDemocratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nGas of India representing the Republic of India\n\n3. The Ministry of Investment of the\n\nUnited Arab Emirates to represent the United Arab Emirates.\n\n(iii) \u2022 The parties will engage in discussion on various projects for the purpose of developing Trincomalee as an Energy Hub and with a view to strengthening energy security for Sri Lanka.\n\n\u2022 The parties will continue discussions on delivery of petroleum products via a petroleum pipeline to be constructed from India to Sri Lanka.\n\n\u2022 The parties also agree to refurbish and where required, to develop allied infrastructure for the Trincomalee Tank Farm (85 tanks - Upper Tank Farm) to create a regional Energy Hub.\n\n\u2022 The parties will also examine the potential to supply bunker fuel from storage for distribution to demand markets.\n\n\u2022 The parties will also engage in discussions on exploring the potential of development of a refinery (hereinafter collectively referred to as \u201cProject\u201d).\n\n(iv) To construct and complete the projects\n\nwithin 36 months from the date of obtaining all statutory and other relevant approvals.\n\n(b) (i) The Government\u2019s objective is to develop\n\nthe China Bay area in Trincomalee into a regional hub for the import, storage and distribution of petroleum products (Energy Hub). Following the establishment of the Energy Hub, a decision will be made on the establishment of multi-product pipeline systems between Sri Lanka and India, based on the infrastructure requirements of the Energy Hub.\n\n1343 1344\n\n\u0db4\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dda\u0db8\u0dca\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\n\n(ii) Of the 61 tanks allocated to the Trinco"
